537
01:20:24.510 --> 01:20:27.630
We were important to all of them in some way.

538
01:20:34.780 --> 01:20:38.250
Guy of Gisborne and Robin Hood

539
01:20:39.890 --> 01:20:41.320
Do you know its story?

540
01:20:46.620 --> 01:20:47.790
Yes.

541
01:20:52.710 --> 01:20:55.150
They say you killed him.

542
01:20:57.220 --> 01:20:58.839
Did you really cut off his head?

543
01:20:58.900 --> 01:21:00.100
You're confused. Leper.

544
01:21:00.180 --> 01:21:01.990
I won't tell anyone.

545
01:21:04.710 --> 01:21:07.990
But don't lie to a
man on his deathbed.

546
01:21:10.260 --> 01:21:13.820
So... did you really cut off his head?

547
01:21:17.320 --> 01:21:19.200
There was no Guy from Gisborne.

548
01:21:20.250 --> 01:21:22.700
Just one of many
tales passed down.

549
01:21:25.110 --> 01:21:26.824
But I cut off the others' heads.

550
01:21:34.410 --> 01:21:36.610
Do you really not remember?

551
01:21:38.790 --> 01:21:39.850
No.

552
01:21:40.960 --> 01:21:43.120
Consider this name.

553
01:21:47.280 --> 01:21:50.100
There was a man from Gisborne.

554
01:21:53.560 --> 01:21:55.650
But you didn't cut off his head.

555
01:21:58.110 --> 01:21:59.920
You cut off his ear.

556
01:22:07.600 --> 01:22:12.700
You said you'd share a
drink with him in another life.

557
01:22:14.780 --> 01:22:16.350
Do you remember this?

558
01:22:28.240 --> 01:22:31.040
It's like we found a different life.

559
01:22:38.420 --> 01:22:43.810
Now... There is a cruelty
that I would like you not to do...

560
01:22:46.440 --> 01:22:50.410
And you will protect
the orchard until you die.

561
01:22:53.670 --> 01:22:56.770
You will serve the Priest and the people of this place...

562
01:22:57.570 --> 01:23:01.270
Sect. past and future.

563
01:23:05.870 --> 01:23:09.900
But at no point in time.

564
01:23:12.220 --> 01:23:16.820
In those beautiful and peaceful years...

565
01:23:19.670 --> 01:23:23.470
Will you tell the Priest
who you really are?

566
01:23:29.270 --> 01:23:30.670
From where?

567
01:23:33.070 --> 01:23:34.470
Because...

568
01:23:36.070 --> 01:23:41.400
One of those nameless. faceless people...
That death in the shadows of your mind...

569
01:23:44.270 --> 01:23:46.200
in another life...

570
01:23:48.840 --> 01:23:50.240
was his beloved.

571
01:23:58.690 --> 01:24:00.100
Promise me.

572
01:24:05.070 --> 01:24:06.470
Robin.

573
01:24:07.970 --> 01:24:09.500
Promise me.

574
01:25:41.070 --> 01:25:42.470
Goodbye. Brigid.

575
01:25:55.860 --> 01:25:57.260
Arthur.

576
01:25:59.420 --> 01:26:00.820
Come on.

577
01:26:03.750 --> 01:26:05.900
There is a child on the far shore.

578
01:26:07.180 --> 01:26:08.580
Maybe it's your nephew.

579
01:26:10.800 --> 01:26:13.350
The leper said he was
looking for his missing nephew.

580
01:26:14.370 --> 01:26:15.370
Yes.

581
01:26:16.370 --> 01:26:19.190
- Could it be him?
- We'll see.

582
01:26:58.070 --> 01:27:00.230
I don't see any traces of anyone.

583
01:27:01.370 --> 01:27:02.830
We must wait.

584
01:27:03.600 --> 01:27:05.170
Maybe they'll come back.

585
01:27:27.230 --> 01:27:28.630
What is your name?

586
01:27:32.480 --> 01:27:33.880
Arthur.

587
01:27:34.980 --> 01:27:37.120
Don't waste your time lying to me.

588
01:27:37.200 --> 01:27:38.630
What is your real name?

589
01:27:43.140 --> 01:27:44.540
Godwyn.

590
01:27:47.600 --> 01:27:53.050
You decide. Godwyn; Will you do

591
01:27:53.450 --> 01:27:55.650
the work yourself or bring your family?

592
01:27:58.370 --> 01:27:59.420
For what job?

593
01:27:59.500 --> 01:28:01.940
How many men have you killed. Godwyn?

594
01:28:03.100 --> 01:28:06.200
How many children did you kill?

595
01:28:11.370 --> 01:28:14.370
I've killed so many
people I can't count them.

596
01:28:16.080 --> 01:28:19.850
For longer than your life; whom I killed a lifetime ago; and

597
01:28:19.940 --> 01:28:22.930
actually I don't even know who he is; I kill people's descendants.

598
01:28:23.020 --> 01:28:25.496
That's me then The ones
that have no meaning for you.

599
01:28:26.690 --> 01:28:31.270
But their siblings and their children
and grandchildren remember me.

600
01:28:32.270 --> 01:28:34.340
And now I must kill them.

601
01:28:35.190 --> 01:28:36.620
Over and over again...

602
01:28:37.830 --> 01:28:41.600
in different forms.
like shadows... again.

603
01:28:42.970 --> 01:28:45.100
And yet it never ends.

604
01:28:48.700 --> 01:28:50.500
It's a curse. Godwyn.

605
01:28:52.410 --> 01:28:56.610
This is something you brought upon
yourself. even if it was done out of duty.

606
01:28:57.630 --> 01:29:00.170
He doesn't care about your duty.

607
01:29:00.630 --> 01:29:03.870
All this world cares about is blood...

608
01:29:05.270 --> 01:29:07.500
and will give in return The
only thing is blood again.

609
01:29:10.380 --> 01:29:12.850
You want to kill a child. Godwin?

610
01:29:15.630 --> 01:29:19.650
Do you want to take responsibility
for the murder of a little girl?

611
01:29:22.810 --> 01:29:24.010
No.

612
01:29:35.980 --> 01:29:37.420
Is your father dead?

613
01:29:38.830 --> 01:29:40.230
What about your uncles?

614
01:29:43.170 --> 01:29:45.100
Only I remained.

615
01:29:49.430 --> 01:29:51.230
Who else lives. Godwyn?

616
01:29:53.400 --> 01:29:54.800
My mother.

617
01:29:56.270 --> 01:29:57.670
My aunts.

618
01:29:58.900 --> 01:30:00.300
My sisters.

619
01:30:00.670 --> 01:30:02.430
You have a home. Godwyn.

620
01:30:04.670 --> 01:30:07.000
- Yes.
- Go home.

621
01:30:08.100 --> 01:30:10.870
Tell your family that all your
blood debts have been paid.

622
01:30:11.430 --> 01:30:13.170
It will all be paid for one day.

623
01:30:15.420 --> 01:30:16.820
Sleep in your own bed.

624
01:30:17.770 --> 01:30:22.030
Value the life you will
share with your loved ones.

625
01:30:23.690 --> 01:30:25.660
And if you come back here...

626
01:30:26.670 --> 01:30:30.570
You'll be wasting this chance
at life that I'm giving you now

627
01:30:31.670 --> 01:30:35.470
and I will cut your throat.
I will never think about it again.

628
01:30:42.200 --> 01:30:43.600
Go now.

629
01:30:45.860 --> 01:30:47.260
Don't look back.

630
01:31:41.820 --> 01:31:43.650
I thought you were gone.

631
01:31:53.540 --> 01:31:55.410
I am an outlaw

My Robin.

632
01:31:58.900 --> 01:32:02.670
You should know that I'm a monster.

633
01:32:04.900 --> 01:32:06.500
I'm not one of the Randolphs.

634
01:32:09.160 --> 01:32:10.830
I am an outlaw...

635
01:32:11.200 --> 01:32:12.600
Robin Hood

636
01:32:14.000 --> 01:32:21.500
Turkish subtitles;
<font color="#ff0000">ufukbaba</font>

637
01:32:27.900 --> 01:32:29.300
I am sad.

638
01:34:29.400 --> 01:34:31.210
Tell me how I should leave.

639
01:34:33.430 --> 01:34:35.000
I will go now.

640
01:34:42.830 --> 01:34:44.230
Get into bed.

641
01:35:04.070 --> 01:35:05.770
- Brigid.
- Lie down..

642
01:38:31.300 --> 01:38:33.500
You burned my husband alive.

643
01:38:38.900 --> 01:38:42.680
I dream that he is already dead.
But why did you bar the door?

644
01:38:47.770 --> 01:38:51.900
Searching for the ashes of
our home seemed like a lifetime.

645
01:38:55.020 --> 01:38:57.120
And it looked so small.

646
01:38:58.960 --> 01:39:02.670
curled up in the corner.
with most of it gone.

647
01:39:07.230 --> 01:39:10.380
And I can't imagine it
enough. I know you're alive.

648
01:39:15.120 --> 01:39:19.800
Because he hugged
our children until the end.

649
01:40:08.000 --> 01:40:09.400
Randolph.

650
01:40:11.600 --> 01:40:13.070
Mine.

651
01:41:07.030 --> 01:41:09.470
People talk about Robin Hood...

652
01:41:14.300 --> 01:41:15.700
They tell stories..

653
01:41:22.270 --> 01:41:23.670
It's all lies.

654
01:41:27.630 --> 01:41:30.390
Lies I told a long time ago...

655
01:41:32.000 --> 01:41:34.000
So these fools...

656
01:41:35.370 --> 01:41:37.300
They followed me into the dark.

657
01:41:46.830 --> 01:41:48.230
Robin.

658
01:41:54.200 --> 01:41:56.370
What are they doing to you?

659
01:42:02.070 --> 01:42:03.770
Don't be afraid.

660
01:42:06.000 --> 01:42:08.700
I will save you from this place.

661
01:42:10.990 --> 01:42:13.060
I will save little Margaret.

662
01:42:14.790 --> 01:42:17.800
We will start a
new life together.

663
01:42:18.500 --> 01:42:19.900
Edward

664
01:42:23.900 --> 01:42:25.870
Tell me about your wife.

665
01:42:35.630 --> 01:42:37.030
My wife...

666
01:42:39.780 --> 01:42:41.180
Margaret.

667
01:42:45.090 --> 01:42:46.490
Margaret.

668
01:42:48.600 --> 01:42:50.830
My wife Margaret.

669
01:42:53.100 --> 01:42:54.630
Draw a portrait.

670
01:42:57.370 --> 01:42:58.770
Should I draw a portrait?

671
01:43:02.970 --> 01:43:04.400
He has hair...

672
01:43:06.490 --> 01:43:07.890
It's like red...

673
01:43:09.300 --> 01:43:11.300
setting sun.

674
01:43:14.300 --> 01:43:17.370
Like the setting summer sun.

675
01:43:24.670 --> 01:43:28.900
Red... like a sinking summer...

676
01:43:29.740 --> 01:43:31.140
Sun...

677
01:43:49.200 --> 01:43:50.200
Robin...

678
01:43:56.500 --> 01:43:58.870
Did you find your correct death?

679
01:44:59.370 --> 01:45:01.470
I'm ready to finish.

680
01:45:08.600 --> 01:45:10.700
I owe this life to you.

681
01:45:18.170 --> 01:45:19.670
Monstrous...

682
01:45:24.230 --> 01:45:26.570
But I owe this life to you.

683
01:45:27.150 --> 01:45:28.674
You don't owe me anything.

684
01:45:33.770 --> 01:45:36.300
I've never taken a life before.

685
01:45:40.400 --> 01:45:43.030
It can be like pruning a flower.

686
01:45:45.320 --> 01:45:46.990
Ok.
It shouldn't be.

687
01:45:47.700 --> 01:45:49.200
It shouldn't be.

688
01:45:50.470 --> 01:45:52.130
But it could happen.

689
01:45:57.630 --> 01:46:00.230
I help those who
come to this island.

690
01:46:03.130 --> 01:46:04.600
I am healing them.

691
01:46:08.310 --> 01:46:09.430
Please.

692
01:46:14.900 --> 01:46:16.400
Heal me.

693
01:47:12.030 --> 01:47:13.470
Little Margaret...

694
01:47:19.270 --> 01:47:21.670
Your father's name was John.

695
01:47:30.870 --> 01:47:36.260
I've known him for many years.
before he became your father.

696
01:47:42.370 --> 01:47:43.770
One day a fast flowing

697
01:47:45.270 --> 01:47:47.400
I was crossing a
bridge over the river.

698
01:47:48.800 --> 01:47:50.830
I met him...

699
01:47:53.630 --> 01:47:55.230
He was stubborn.

700
01:47:58.170 --> 01:48:00.430
He would not surrender.

701
01:48:02.370 --> 01:48:04.000
Not to anyone.

702
01:48:05.030 --> 01:48:07.000
Not even to me.

703
01:48:09.900 --> 01:48:13.900
We also wrestled on that bridge.

704
01:48:15.910 --> 01:48:18.780
He's hitting back and forth.

705
01:48:20.970 --> 01:48:23.800
I hit him on the side of his head.

706
01:48:26.100 --> 01:48:28.520
He hit me in the stomach.

707
01:48:29.630 --> 01:48:32.230
I stumbled on that bridge.

708
01:48:33.810 --> 01:48:35.210
I fell into the water.

709
01:48:36.290 --> 01:48:38.190
He dropped me on my butt.

710
01:48:42.470 --> 01:48:44.700
When I drag myself out...

711
01:48:45.630 --> 01:48:47.030
I was soaked to the bone...

712
01:48:48.950 --> 01:48:50.410
We hugged.

713
01:48:53.770 --> 01:48:57.570
We named your father Little John.

714
01:48:59.230 --> 01:49:01.400
And the outlaws in Greenwood

715
01:49:04.600 --> 01:49:07.870
As. we have lived for many years...

716
01:49:11.370 --> 01:49:12.770
We had holidays.

717
01:49:15.810 --> 01:49:19.640
We gave silver to the humble.

718
01:49:36.770 --> 01:49:38.770
But we stole that silver.

719
01:49:44.800 --> 01:49:46.200
her bad

720
01:49:49.470 --> 01:49:50.970
We stole from people...

721
01:49:55.600 --> 01:49:57.000
Do you understand?

722
01:49:59.570 --> 01:50:00.970
Bad people.

723
01:50:16.000 --> 01:50:17.400
Your father...

724
01:50:18.660 --> 01:50:20.580
He wanted me to tell you...

725
01:50:26.460 --> 01:50:28.760
Because he loved you very much. my dear.

726
01:50:33.050 --> 01:50:35.450
You should never tell anyone.

727
01:50:37.160 --> 01:50:39.660
Even to the kids you play with.

728
01:50:40.970 --> 01:50:44.970
You should never tell them your father's name.

729
01:50:48.970 --> 01:50:51.230
There are bad people out there.

730
01:50:53.830 --> 01:50:57.470
And they're angry at your father.

731
01:51:01.810 --> 01:51:04.180
That's why they're angry at you too.

732
01:51:09.000 --> 01:51:11.030
Can we keep this secret?

733
01:51:13.630 --> 01:51:16.230
I can keep this
secret Little Margaret.

734
01:51:18.780 --> 01:51:20.180
Can you?

735
01:51:24.290 --> 01:51:25.690
Good morning my baby.

736
01:51:28.230 --> 01:51:29.830
Come to me now.

737
01:51:39.830 --> 01:51:41.230
Take this.

738
01:51:42.920 --> 01:51:44.480
Why did they call it small?

739
01:51:45.250 --> 01:51:46.650
What?

740
01:51:47.650 --> 01:51:49.810
Why was my father called "Little"?

741
01:51:55.640 --> 01:51:58.170
Because it was small when I found it.

742
01:51:59.770 --> 01:52:01.170
Like you.

743
01:52:09.150 --> 01:52:10.550
String it up.

744
01:52:33.520 --> 01:52:36.720
Bend with your leg.
like you see me do.

745
01:52:57.950 --> 01:52:59.350
Go to the window.

746
01:53:23.630 --> 01:53:25.030
Insert the arrow into the bowstring.

747
01:53:33.630 --> 01:53:38.500
Find a spot where the
waters meet the sky.

748
01:53:43.570 --> 01:53:45.900
Read it to the fullest...

749
01:53:49.600 --> 01:53:51.000
And wait.

750
01:53:52.770 --> 01:53:55.030
I'll tell you when to relax.

751
01:53:58.030 --> 01:53:59.570
And when I do this...

752
01:54:00.460 --> 01:54:02.290
you don't let go...

753
01:54:04.970 --> 01:54:07.570
You don't even hold it anymore.

754
01:54:14.790 --> 01:54:16.320
Watch out for that target.

755
01:54:19.670 --> 01:54:22.100
Your body will always be in motion.

756
01:54:25.370 --> 01:54:29.830
Feel when the arrow will fly correctly.

757
01:54:33.080 --> 01:54:34.950
You will find a dance.

758
01:54:37.470 --> 01:54:39.900
Wait until I tell you to quit...

759
01:54:43.460 --> 01:54:45.060
You are strong.

760
01:54:46.200 --> 01:54:47.600
Feel...

761
01:54:49.400 --> 01:54:50.800
Don't swing...

762
01:54:54.230 --> 01:54:55.630
That dance...

763
01:55:02.630 --> 01:55:04.030
Now relax.
